docs/papers187_191_sequence/scouting/algebra_lane/replacement/KILL_LEDGER.md-15-| `R05/CSW` | Pure fixed points and two-cycles; all fibres have size one. | `KILL_INVOLUTION_ACTION_ONLY` | The update is an involution because commutation is swap-invariant.  A commuting-pair census is static group theory, not a second dynamical theorem. |
docs/papers187_191_sequence/scouting/algebra_lane/replacement/KILL_LEDGER.md-16-| `R06/MGR` | `T^3=1`; `F_2^3` gives 344 fixed states and 56 three-cycles, while `F_3^3` gives 8,451 fixed states and 3,744 three-cycles; all fibres are one. | `KILL_RANK_GATE_ACTION_ONLY` | Rank merely gates identity versus cyclic coordinate rotation.  Gaussian full-rank counting plus a permutation action is below the value floor. |
docs/papers187_191_sequence/scouting/algebra_lane/replacement/KILL_LEDGER.md:17:| `R07/IAV` | Four constant fixed states; maximum tails `4,6,7,8` for lengths `3..6` at cap three; fibre histograms vary irregularly. | `KILL_CONSENSUS_OWNER_NO_INVERSE` | Integer floor averaging is in the consensus/quantized-averaging surface.  The sum Lyapunov function is not an exact all-parameter clock, and no independent labelled inverse law survived. |
docs/papers187_191_sequence/scouting/algebra_lane/replacement/KILL_LEDGER.md-18-| `R08/PFR` | All 5,461 words reach their ordinary reduced word; maximum parallel depth three; 1,457 fixed reduced words. | `KILL_DIRECT_FREE_REDUCTION` | Parallel deletion changes only the reduction schedule.  The normal form and inverse-word enumeration remain standard free-group rewriting, so the clock cannot support a paper. |
docs/papers187_191_sequence/scouting/algebra_lane/replacement/KILL_LEDGER.md-19-| `R09/RPX` | Rectangular bands `2x2` and `2x3` give only fixed points and two-cycles, with singleton fibres. | `KILL_PRODUCT_EXCHANGE_INVOLUTION` | The identity `(xy,yx)^2=(x,y)` is an immediate rectangular-band calculation.  This is thinner than already rejected group product-exchange systems. |
docs/papers187_191_sequence/scouting/algebra_lane/replacement/KILL_LEDGER.md-20-| `R10/BPA` | On `B_2^m`, recurrent count is always three, maximum tail is `m`, and the zero target dominates the fibre histogram. | `KILL_ZERO_PROPAGATION_NO_ATLAS` | Matrix-unit index mismatch merely propagates zero through local products.  Beyond the fixed diagonal words, no uniform target theorem independent of the compatibility-path engine emerged. |
